# HTTPS only for public URLs (xboard-api)

Treat **browser-facing and mail** URLs as **HTTPS only**. Do not design flows around `http://` for production.

## Do

- Set **`APP_URL`** with an `https://` base in every deployed environment (staging, production). Tests may use a dedicated fake host (e.g. `https://api.xboard.test` in `phpunit.xml`).
- When building links for **email or operator web pages**, ensure the scheme is `https://` (e.g. `App\Support\PublicHttpsUrl::upgradeMailBaseToHttps()` on a host base before `URL::temporarySignedRoute` or string concatenation).
- Behind a reverse proxy / TLS terminator, fix scheme via **`TrustProxies`** / forwarded headers so Laravel sees HTTPS correctly — not via blind redirects.

## Do not

- **Do not** add global or route middleware that redirects “every HTTP request to HTTPS” inside the app. Behind TLS termination the app often receives **HTTP internally**; that pattern causes **redirect loops** (“too many redirects”) and breaks signed mail links.
- **Do not** assume operators will “open the http link first”; links in mail must already be `https://`.

## Signed operator links

Signed URLs include the scheme. Generate them with an **`https://` root** once; do not rely on a second hop (redirect) to “upgrade” the request.
